emma: Quick flag for the SDK team — customers keep tripping over imports when using the app router + client components. Error they paste: "ReferenceError: require is not defined" or "fs is not found" from our bundle on Vercel Edge.

lee: that's usually the resolver picking the Node/CJS entry instead of the ESM/browser entry. Do we have a browser/worker entry in package.json?

emma: no, package.json currently only has main + module. We ship dist/node (cjs), dist/esm, and dist/edge but no conditional exports.

oliver: two pragmatic options: (A) make explicit subpath entries so users can import 'sdk/server' or 'sdk/edge' or (B) add conditional exports for node/import/worker/browser so bundlers pick the right file automatically. I prefer both.

lee: example exports I usually add: 
```
"exports": {
  "./*": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/*.js",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/*.js",
    "browser": "./dist/browser/*.js",
    "worker": "./dist/edge/*.js"
  },
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/index.js",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js",
    "browser": "./dist/browser/index.js",
    "worker": "./dist/edge/index.js"
  }
}
```
This helps Vite/Next/webpack pick worker/browser for edge bundling.

emma: good. For DX we should also provide a named import path: `import { createClient } from 'sdk/edge'` so people have an explicit option and don't accidentally import the server build.

oliver: yep. And we should avoid any top-level references to `process`, `fs`, or `globalThis.require`. Even `process.env` at module scope can trigger polyfills. Move those into factory functions or lazily read `process.env` inside server-only helpers.

lee: TS gotchas too: folks reported intellisense pointing to cjs types which breaks ESM import signatures. Add a root "types" pointer and also typesVersions mapping for modern TS: 
```
"types": "dist/types/index.d.ts",
"typesVersions": { ">=4.7": { "*": [ "dist/types/*" ] } }
```
and ensure rollup/tsc outputs .d.ts for each entry file.

emma: Next-specific note: if you import the SDK directly into a client component (files with `use client`), Next will try to bundle it into the client and fail. We should document the recommended patterns: server components, server actions, or API routes. Provide examples for each.

oliver: small sample for server action pattern: 
```
// app/actions/generate.ts (server action)
'use server'
import { createClient } from 'sdk/edge'
export async function generate(prompt) {
  const c = createClient({ apiKey: process.env.SDK_KEY });
  return c.generate(prompt);
}
```
Then call that action from a client component. Keeps SDK out of the browser bundle.

lee: Also add a clear runtime check in the Node build that errors fast with actionable guidance. Something like: 
```
if (typeof fetch === 'undefined' && typeof process !== 'undefined' && process.title !== 'browser') {
  // we're probably in Node server - OK
} else if (typeof window !== 'undefined' || typeof self !== 'undefined') {
  throw new Error('Imported the server SDK in a browser/edge runtime. Use `import from "sdk/edge"` or the documented server action pattern.');
}
```
But be careful to keep checks tiny and not add Node builtin requires.

emma: CI-wise let's add matrix tests that bundle the example with Next/edge target + Node server target + webpack 5 to catch resolver regressions. Also add an ESLint rule in the example app that flags importing from 'sdk' inside `app/**` files that start with `use client`. Could be a small custom rule or a plugin config.

oliver: one more: Next's edge bundler sometimes treats conditional exports weirdly. As a fallback, include a lightweight browser UMD build under dist/browser and set the "browser" field in package.json to it. That helps older bundlers.

qa: we'll write a repro harness that replicates the Vercel Edge case and attach to a ticket. Repro steps: create app-router app, add `use client` component that imports `createClient` directly, deploy to edge. Expect bundle error.

build-bot: created issue DEVEX-347: "Next app-router: package exports + explicit edge/server entrypoints + DX docs" assigned @oliver.

emma: action items: 1) oliver to add conditional exports + browser field + edge subpath; 2) lee to add runtime guard and update build scripts to emit dist/edge; 3) qa to add CI bundle matrix and repro; 4) docs team to add migration note and example snippets.

oliver: I'll open a PR with the package.json changes and a small example under examples/next-approuter-edge. Will also add typesVersion mapping and publish a canary tag so we can validate with users.

emma: perfect. Thanks everyone — this should reduce onboarding friction a lot. :rocket:
